        "Content": "Shangarry — A Landmark Irish Residence of Heritage & Modern Luxury \r\n\r\nShangarry, Gurtymadden is an extraordinary country estate combining heritage, craftsmanship, and modern comfort across 395 m² of refined living space, set within 2.64 hectares (6.5 acres) of landscaped grounds. This remarkable property is a faithful replica of the original 1641 dwelling, built with meticulous attention to historical detail while integrating contemporary luxury throughout. The result is a residence of rare character, where authentic period features — including the original 1641 fireplace and original kitchen flagstones — coexist seamlessly with highquality modern finishes. \r\n\r\nApproached through mature greenery and expansive lawns, the estate immediately conveys a sense of privacy and tranquillity. Its most exceptional feature is the private, springfed wild brown trout lake, a natural jewel that elevates the property far beyond a typical rural home. The lake is complemented by a bespoke Lakehouse bar, creating a unique setting for entertaining, relaxation, and lakeside gatherings. This combination of private water, curated outdoor spaces, and heritage architecture makes Shangarry one of the most distinctive residential offerings in the region. Inside, the home is generous and beautifully balanced. \r\n\r\nWith five large ensuite bedrooms, the residence is designed for comfort, privacy, and flexibility. The scale of the rooms, the quality of materials, and the thoughtful layout support both family living and sophisticated entertaining. Every space reflects the estate’s commitment to craftsmanship — from bespoke joinery and natural timber floors to carefully restored heritage elements that anchor the home in its historical context. \r\n\r\nThe grounds are equally impressive. Mature landscaping, natural planting, and wide open lawns frame the residence and lake, creating a serene environment ideal for outdoor living. Whether enjoyed for fishing, lakeside dining, morning walks, or evening gatherings at the Lakehouse bar, the estate offers a lifestyle that is both restorative and richly atmospheric. The property feels secluded yet connected, offering complete privacy while remaining within easy reach of Loughrea, Galway City, and key transport links. Shangarry is more than a home — it is a private rural sanctuary with deep historical roots, exceptional craftsmanship, and a suite of lifestyle amenities rarely found in a private residence. Its combination of acreage, architectural authenticity, private lake, and substantial interior space positions it as a truly unique estate in the Galway countryside. \r\n\r\nProperty Highlights \r\n- Faithful replica of the original 1641 residence \r\n- Original 1641 fireplace and flagstone kitchen floor \r\n- Five large ensuite bedrooms \r\n- Oak herringbone flooring throughout \r\n- Lakehouse Bar with cinema screen, stone fireplace, BBQ, decking \r\n- 400yearold Irish oak trees and landscaped grounds \r\n- Fully stocked springfed lake \r\n- Restored stone coach house \r\n- Underfloor heating, pumped cavity insulation, hollowcore concrete floors \r\n- 11 Smart TVs, 500mb NBI fibre, 20kv backup generator**\r\n - BER B2 \r\n\r\nAccommodation \r\n\r\nEntrance \r\nLiving Room (9.5m x 6.0m) A dramatic welcome space featuring oak herringbone floors, the original 1641 fireplace, and custom skirting, architrave and panelling. \r\nKitchen (9.5m x 9.0m) A remarkable blend of old and new: the original 1641 stone floor, Rangemaster cooker, centre island, fitted cabinetry and westfacing patio doors opening to a brick terrace. \r\nUtility & Wet Room Fully fitted utility and a fully tiled wet room with shower. \r\nSitting Room / Viewing Room (5.8m x 5.3m) Dual smart TVs (65” & 85”), oak herringbone floor, solid fuel stove, custom furniture and terrace access. \r\n\r\nBedrooms \r\nBedroom 1 (Ground Floor) Cinema screen, ensuite, and patio access. \r\nBedroom 2 Walkin wardrobe, sauna, yoga/gym room and a luxurious ensuite with rolltop bath. \r\nBedroom 3 Walkin wardrobe and fully tiled ensuite. \r\nBedroom 4 Fitted wardrobe and ensuite/dressing room with bath and shower. \r\nBedroom 5 Large ensuite/dressing room with walkin shower. \r\n\r\nLakehouse Bar (6.7m x 4.5m) A signature feature of Shangarry — a purposebuilt bar overlooking the lake, complete with cinema screen, stone fireplace, BBQ, extraction unit, stone floor, pine ceiling and expansive decking. A private retreat for entertaining, dining and lakeside enjoyment. \r\n\r\nExternal Features \r\n- Gravelled driveways and patios \r\n- Mature paddocks \r\n- Restored stone coach house\r\n- Electric gated entrance \r\n- 400yearold Irish oak trees"
      },
